From: Andreas Stieger <Andreas.Stieger@gmx.de>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:10:40 +0100
Subject: [patch] fix version macro for tests
Upstream: no (it's obsolete with every release)

FAIL: test_mhd_version
[...]
Checking MHD_get_version() function vs MHD_VERSION macro.
'1.0.11' vs '0x01001000' ('1.0.10') - FAILED.

Index: libmicrohttpd-1.0.11/src/include/microhttpd.h
===================================================================
--- libmicrohttpd-1.0.11.orig/src/include/microhttpd.h
+++ libmicrohttpd-1.0.11/src/include/microhttpd.h
@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ MHD_C_DECLRATIONS_START_HERE_
  * they are parsed as decimal numbers.
  * Example: 0x01093001 = 1.9.30-1.
  */
-#define MHD_VERSION 0x01001000
+#define MHD_VERSION 0x01001100
 
 /* If generic headers don't work on your platform, include headers
    which define 'va_list', 'size_t', 'ssize_t', 'intptr_t', 'off_t',
